Martin Read <mpread@chiark.greenend.org.uk> writes:
> 5parrow <mail.gatech@gtg692n.edu> wrote:
> >Begs a question. Does Rodney resist polymorph? I know MR protects vs. 
> >death and polymorph, but Rodney isn't death-resistant so...
> 
> *Monster* magic resistance does not protect against death rays; monsters
> are only protected from death rays if they are undead, demonic, or
> protected by an item of magic resistance or reflection.  Monster magic
> resistance provides a chance of resisting polymorph.

This is slightly misleading. There are two completely different things
that are easily confused: a magic resistance saving throw (which
doesn't help against death rays, but does against polymorph) and the
plain ordinary magic resistance intrinsic (which protects against
both). All monsters have a saving throw (which may have a base value
of 0, but which will be adjusted for level); the only monsters with
the magic resistance intrinsic are those who have an item conferring
it, those who have a magic missile attack, and baby grey dragons.

(Also, it's being non-living rather than just undead that provides an
alternative defence against death rays, which additionally includes
vortices, golems, and manes.)

